    bestFor: "Mandarin speakers and learners, and Indian businesses working closely with Chinese suppliers who need a strong Chinese-language assistant.",
    notFor: "Almost every ordinary Indian user, who will get more from DeepSeek, Qwen, Gemini or ChatGPT with far less friction and no access barrier.",
    verdict: "Doubao is a genuinely capable assistant that happens to be built for a market that is not India. It leads on Chinese-language quality and rock-bottom API pricing, but the Chinese-only interface, the Chinese phone number requirement, the absence of Indic language support and the lack of open weights make it impractical for Indian users. Unless you specifically need Chinese, choose DeepSeek or Qwen instead.",
    faq: [
      { q: "Is Doubao available in India?", a: "Not in any practical sense. Doubao is a China-first product, its apps are not distributed through Indian app stores the way global assistants are, and registration generally expects a Chinese mobile number. The website is reachable but the interface is entirely in Chinese. Most Indian users who try to sign up stop at the phone verification step." },
      { q: "Is Doubao free?", a: "Yes, the consumer Doubao assistant is free in China, with no paid tier an Indian user would encounter, since it is not sold internationally. API access through ByteDance's Volcano Engine cloud is billed per million tokens in Chinese yuan at very low rates, but account verification is built for Chinese businesses, which makes price largely academic for Indian developers." },
      { q: "Does Doubao support Hindi?", a: "No, not to any useful standard. Doubao is built for Chinese users and its language strength is Mandarin, with adequate English as a secondary. Hindi output is unreliable and other Indian languages such as Bengali, Tamil, Telugu, Marathi and Gujarati are not realistic options. For Indian language work, use Gemini or an Indic-specific model instead." },
      { q: "Is Doubao safe to use, and where is my data stored?", a: "Data processed by Doubao is handled in China and falls under Chinese law, including the Data Security Law and cooperation obligations with no Indian equivalent. Unlike DeepSeek and Qwen there are no open weights to self-host, so this cannot be engineered around. Do not put Indian client data, employer information or personal identity documents into it." },
      { q: "Is Doubao banned in India?", a: "Doubao itself has not been the subject of a specific public ban, but it is effectively inaccessible to most Indian users because of its Chinese registration requirements. Its parent ByteDance has had apps including TikTok blocked in India since June 2020 on national security grounds, and many Indian employers name ByteDance products explicitly in internal restriction lists." },
      { q: "Doubao vs DeepSeek, which should an Indian user pick?", a: "DeepSeek, without much hesitation. It has an English interface, is directly accessible from India with no phone verification barrier, offers open weights you can self-host in India, and delivers stronger reasoning and coding. Doubao's advantages, Chinese-language quality and voice, only matter if you actually work in Chinese. For everything else DeepSeek is the practical choice." },
      { q: "Doubao vs ChatGPT for Indian users?", a: "ChatGPT wins comprehensively for Indian users. It is available here, works in English and reasonable Hindi, has Indian rupee-adjacent pricing at roughly Rs 1,700 a month for the paid tier, a free tier that most people find sufficient, apps on Indian app stores and a vast ecosystem. Doubao offers none of that outside China." },
      { q: "How much does the Doubao API cost?", a: "ByteDance prices Doubao API access through Volcano Engine per million tokens in Chinese yuan, at rates widely reported as among the cheapest in the market, likely equivalent to well under Rs 100 per million input tokens. That conversion is indicative and largely theoretical for Indian developers, since Volcano Engine account verification is oriented towards Chinese businesses and support is in Chinese." },
      { q: "Is there a Doubao app for Android or iPhone in India?", a: "Official Doubao apps exist for Android and iOS but are distributed primarily through Chinese app stores and Chinese account regions. Indian users generally cannot install them through normal Play Store or App Store listings. Beware of unofficial APK files claiming to be Doubao, as sideloading unverified builds of any assistant is a serious security risk." },
      { q: "Can Doubao be used for business in India?", a: "It is a poor fit. There is no Indian billing, no local support, no rupee pricing, no Indian partner ecosystem, a Chinese-only console, and unavoidable Chinese data residency with no self-hosting option. Indian firms in banking, insurance, listed companies and government-linked sectors will typically find it prohibited by internal policy. Use DeepSeek, Qwen, Gemini or ChatGPT instead." },
    ],
